ull,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.09109695186589217,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.034929909019868574,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":49.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0037854373425616483,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":45.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0277333514819478,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":53.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.04547,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":30.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bank of Marin Bancorp operates as the holding company for Bank of Marin that provides a range of financial services to small to medium-sized businesses, not-for-profit organizations, and commercial real estate investors in the United States. The company offers personal and business checking and savings accounts; and individual retirement, health savings, and demand deposit marketplace accounts, as well as time certificates of deposit, certificate of deposit account registry, and insured cash sweep services. It also provides commercial real estate, commercial and industrial, small business, and consumer loans, as well as construction financing and home equity lines of credit. In addition, the company offers merchant and payroll services; commercial equipment leasing program; payment solutions; treasury management services; credit cards; automated teller machines; and mobile deposit, remote deposit capture, automated clearing house, wire transfer, and image lockbox services. Further, it provides wealth management and trust services comprising customized investment portfolio management, trust administration, estate settlement, and custody services; international banking; and telephone and digital banking services. The company was founded in 1989 and is headquartered in Novato, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy D. Myers | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 312 people. Revenue per employee of $94K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, declining at 6%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $119K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Bank of Marin Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $462M market cap on $29M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -40% over the past three years and -9% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -15.3pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $37M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 127 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -15.3pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 161% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 208% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Stephens Forecasts Strong Price Appreciation for Bank of Marin Bancorp (NASDAQ:BMRC) Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/stephens-forecasts-strong-price-appreciation-for-bank-of-marin-bancorp-nasdaqbmrc-stock.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793644254.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"